display-credit-balance-in-statusline

Lane: frontend

Unit: present-account-quota-in-statusline

ChildPatch: display-credit-balance-in-statusline

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Present account credits and time-relative quota consumption in the TUI status line using the existing authoritative account snapshots.

Requires: Unit:frontend/control-model-and-reasoning-with-keyboard

Provides: An independently selectable default credit-balance item shares the status-card value without adding queries or mixing thread consumption; TUI quota windows show compact duration, remaining quota, pace and meaningful usage rate with severity colors, matching live previews and preserving setup examples when data is unavailable.

Boundary: Own status-line presentation and retained reset timing for quota calculations. Preserve native snapshot selection, account refresh, authentication, status cards, terminal titles, other interface modes and independent thread-usage accounting. Omit unknown live values without placeholders or separators and add no polling or account-specific rendering branches.

Verification: Focused configuration-schema, credit selection, live/setup-preview parity, account-source isolation, query independence, same-window pace, unavailable timing, duration labels, severity styling and other-mode tests.


